  "live_records": {
    "q-145622": {
      "dom_id": "step-q145622",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}, & {x}^{2}\\le y\\le 1,\\,0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}(1-{x}^{2}), & 0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ for $0<x<1.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3}{2})}{\\frac{3}{2}(1-{x}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}^{2}\\le y\\le 1,\\,0<x<1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$\n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}y\\cdot \\,\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{{x}^{2}}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}[\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1-{x}^{4}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\cancel{1-{x}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{(1-{x}^{2})}(1+{x}^{2})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+{x}^{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
