    "q-146353": {
      "dom_id": "step-q146353",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2+y-x}{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5-2x}{6}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{2+y-x}{3})}{(\\frac{5-2x}{6})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(2+y-x)}{5-2x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$\n\nNow, substituting $x=1$ into the expression for ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)=\\frac{2(2+y-1)}{5-2\\cdot 1}=\\frac{2(1+y)}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot \\frac{2(1+y)}{3}\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(y+{y}^{2})\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}[(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{3})-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
